VIOLATION under rule-authoring.md — four breaches, all inside the single numbered clause.

First, MUST-1 and the MUST NOT § "Hedging phrases in a MUST clause". The clause HEADING
states an obligation ("MUST Be Retired In The Confirming Session") while the BODY hedges
throughout — "should generally remove", "is encouraged to move toward", "usually less good",
"tends to be worth avoiding", "may reasonably" — and its closing sentence RETURNS the very
case the heading forbids: a session "may reasonably leave the flag standing and file the
removal for later". The heading is also softened at the premise, "served most of its traffic
through the bake window" where the obligation is 100% through the whole window.

Second, MUST-2 (linguistic tripwires enumerated VERBATIM). The BLOCKED heading is present but
holds six abstract category labels — "Rollback-optimism bias regarding recent launches",
"Ticket-displacement deferral patterns", "Ownership-diffusion reasoning" — instead of the
literal first-person sentences a session emits. A corpus of taxonomy terms traps nothing,
because no session ever writes those words.

Third, MUST-3 (DO / DO NOT examples). The two arms of the worked block are the SAME LINE.
Both delete the check, the dead branch and the config entry, with identical text; only the
trailing adverbs differ, "decisively" against "hesitantly". The contrast slot is filled and
carries no contrast, so the blocked pattern is never shown.

Fourth, MUST-4 and the MUST NOT § "Rationale paragraphs longer than 2 sentences". The
clause's justification runs to three sentences and wanders into flag-evaluation mechanics,
test sharing between paths, how many services read the config, whether the rollback story was
written down, and per-team variation.

Shared surface that is NOT a finding: the frontmatter, the title, the `## MUST Rules`
heading, the numbered clause's HEADING text, the whole `## MUST NOT` section including its
one-sentence justification, the entire Trust-Posture Wiring block with its eight canonical
fields and its structurally-grounded Phase-2 deferral, and the `## Origin` are shared
byte-for-byte with the sibling pole — 506 bytes of head and 2270 bytes of tail. A judge naming
any of them, or naming the deferred detector, the fictional subject, or `priority: 10`, has
scored furniture rather than content. Measured sizes: 4565 bytes here against 4184 on the
sibling, a ratio of 1.091, with an identical ordered `## ` heading list (MUST Rules / MUST
NOT / Trust Posture Wiring / Origin), one numbered clause each, two justification lines each
and one worked block each.
